# What `vercel deploy` from this computer does NOT upload. The Vercel CLI does not read .gitignore,
# only this file (plus its own defaults: .git, node_modules, .next, .env.local, .env.*.local ...).
#
# The photos in public/mock-assets and public/our-story ARE uploaded on purpose: the client preview
# must look exactly like the local site. It is deployed from this computer (never via GitHub, where
# the repo is public) and protected by SITE_PASSWORD.

# Secrets: keys go into Vercel's environment variables, never into an upload.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local build output, server-branch leftovers, test artefacts, tooling
.next-test
server
storage
brag-output*
.claude
.tresor
tests
*.tsbuildinfo
**/__pycache__
